---
description: Lectum frontend architecture and Builder usage rules
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

Builder references are visual guidance only. Do not treat generated code as final product code.

Always follow the existing Lectum frontend architecture:

- Next.js App Router pages live in `src/app/{route}/page.tsx`.
- Route logic lives in `src/app/{route}/logic.tsx`.
- Route forms live in `src/app/{route}/use-form.tsx` when needed.
- API HTTP calls live in `src/api/req/{domain}/index.ts`.
- React Query hooks live in `src/api/callers/{domain}/index.tsx`.
- Query keys live in `src/api/cache/keys.ts`.
- Shared route shells live in `src/templates`.
- Reuse `src/registry/new-york-v4/ui` and `src/components/ui` before creating new UI.

Do not create:

- a parallel API client;
- a parallel auth/session system;
- fake users or mocked endpoints;
- new state management outside the existing Redux Persist/session flow;
- new design tokens per screen.

Use Builder/prototype images to infer layout, hierarchy, spacing, states and copy. Implement with real Lectum components, Tailwind CSS 4, React Hook Form, Zod, TanStack Query and the existing session architecture.

If a screen requires backend data, stop and define the backend contract instead of hardcoding fake data.
